---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Decision from "../../components/Decision.astro";
import { auditSummary, projectHypothesis } from "../../lib/research";
const summary = await auditSummary();
const hypothesis = await projectHypothesis();
const sections = [
  "Question",
  "Intuition",
  "Planned Method",
  "Audit Findings",
  "Decision",
  "Reopen Conditions",
];
---

<Layout title="EXP-001" section="experiments">
  <section class="page-heading">
    <a class="breadcrumb" href="/experiments/">
      ← Experiments
    </a>
    <p class="eyebrow">EXP-001 · Research explanation</p>
    <h1>
      Can attention add
      <br />
      <span class="muted">predictive information?</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A completed feasibility audit and a conditional plan for a historical
      forecasting comparison.
    </p>
  </section>
  <Decision compact />
  <div class="reader-layout section-space">
    <aside class="contents">
      <p class="eyebrow">In this experiment</p>
      <nav aria-label="Experiment sections">
        {sections.map((title) => (
          <a href={"#" + title.toLowerCase().replaceAll(" ", "-")}>{title}</a>
        ))}
      </nav>
      <a class="text-link" href="/methods/">
        Open source reports ↗
      </a>
    </aside>
    <div class="explanation">
      <section id="question">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / Question</p>
        <h2>Does past attention help forecast pending listings?</h2>
        <p>{hypothesis}</p>
        <a href="/methods/protocol/#hypothesis-and-forecast-clock">
          Source: hypothesis and forecast clock
        </a>
      </section>
      <section id="intuition">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Intuition</p>
        <h2>A signal across two platforms.</h2>
        <p>
          The proposed comparison tests whether past relative listing attention
          contains incremental predictive information about newly pending
          activity. Realtor.com measures attention per property relative to the
          U.S.; Zillow measures listings transitioning to pending.
        </p>
        <p>
          Viewer-to-purchase links are unobserved. This cannot estimate
          conversion, willingness to pay or a causal effect of changing
          attention.
        </p>
        <a href="/methods/audit/#what-the-sources-measure">
          Source: what the sources measure
        </a>
      </section>
      <section id="planned-method">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / Planned Method · Not run</p>
        <h2>A matched forecasting comparison.</h2>
        <p>
          The conditional protocol proposes a seasonal naive reference, a
          regularized autoregression with controls, and an attention-augmented
          ridge model. The primary horizon is one month; three months is
          secondary.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every feature must be available at the forecast origin. Models would
          share metros, origins, targets and availability masks. The planned
          evaluation uses count MAE and paired time-block uncertainty. A latent
          sequential extension is conditional on the simple comparison passing a
          stopping rule and requires a fresh evaluation window.
        </p>
        <a href="/methods/protocol/">Read the full conditional specification</a>
      </section>
      <section id="audit-findings">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 / Audit Findings · Completed</p>
        <h2>Overlap is measurable. Eligibility is unresolved.</h2>
        <p>{summary.decision}</p>
        <a href="/methods/audit/">Read the full audit and provenance</a>
      </section>
      <section id="decision">
        <p class="eyebrow">05 / Decision</p>
        <h2>NO-GO at the data feasibility gate.</h2>
        <p>
          The historical forecasting experiment has not been activated. No model
          comparison or forecast accuracy is available. Passing a legacy county
          screen does not verify the geographic footprint of the historical
          series; a revised snapshot does not recover what was known at a past
          origin.
        </p>
        <a href="/methods/audit/#availability-at-prediction-time">
          Source: availability at prediction time
        </a>
      </section>
      <section id="reopen-conditions">
        <p class="eyebrow">06 / Reopen Conditions</p>
        <h2>Verify geography and the information clock.</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Tie Zillow pending and any included control geographies to dated
            county sets.
          </li>
          <li>
            Reconstruct historical feature values from dated releases at each
            forecast cutoff.
          </li>
          <li>
            A prospective archive could support a future test after sufficient
            follow-up.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          A later-release lag alone cannot remove retrospective revisions. The
          protocol remains frozen conditional on GO.
        </p>
        <a href="/methods/audit/#availability-at-prediction-time">
          Source: audit decision and reopening conditions
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
